-- =============================================================================
-- 295_industry_benchmarks_seed.sql
-- Markets page (F11, Scouting + opportunity index) and the Reports suite: first
-- seed of ref.industry_benchmarks (64 rows). Owner approved filling the table from
-- the 2026-10 market research.
--
-- Source of every value
--   docs/sessions/2026-10-15/markets/research/research-dtc-markets.md (sections 3, 4,
--   7) and the pages it cites, re-read on 2026-10-15, plus a few extra pages for the
--   country gaps (Lebesgue CPM, IRP Commerce GB, Statista, Eightx current edition).
--   source_url on every row, as_of = 2026-10-15, vendor pages say so in `note`.
--   Where a page changed since the research was written, the page wins:
--     Statista global CVR is now 1.3 % (Q2 2026), Eightx repeat ranges were revised,
--     the Antyweb PL COD figure is now 24 % of respondents (a user share, not an order
--     share, so not entered).
--   Not entered because the source gives no usable number or definition: Blockify
--   country CVR (counts any conversion), Dynamic Yield AOV (definition and stat
--   unclear), DE return rate ("almost one in four", no figure), ECDB fashion returns,
--   Amp CAC (undated), AdAmigo global CPM (no source).
--
-- Conventions used (runbooks/31_reporting_benchmarks.md, plus three extensions)
--   * Fractions for percents, money with `currency`, one row per source, never an
--     average of two sources.
--   * stat = 'range' for sources that publish only a range: value_low / value_high
--     carry the range and `value` is the arithmetic midpoint, said in `note` on
--     every such row. The Reports loader only reads median / mean / p25 / p75, so it
--     skips these rows by design; the Markets page reads the band.
--   * region holds ISO country codes (SK, PL, HU, DE, AT, GB, IE, CA) next to the
--     runbook's CZ / CEE / EU / US / GLOBAL. Reports never matches them (no client has
--     such a region); ops.v_benchmark_issues (252, not deployed) would flag them and
--     'range' as invalid, so 252 needs both lists extended before it ships.
--   * New metric ids cvr (orders / sessions), cod_share (share of orders or customers
--     paying cash on delivery), return_rate (share of orders returned). They are not in
--     dashboard/lib/reports/registry/ids.ts, so Reports ignores them and Data Health
--     lists them until they are registered. repeat_rate_365 exists but is not
--     benchmarkable, so Reports ignores it too.
--   * Undated sources: period_start = period_end = publish date, said in definition_note.
--   * Triple Whale rows use region US: its base is mostly US brands (not US-only).
--
-- metric_ids used: aov, cod_share, cvr, meta_conversion_rate, meta_cpa, meta_cpm, meta_ctr, meta_roas, repeat_rate_365, return_rate
--
-- Idempotent: MERGE keyed on benchmark_id. A rerun refreshes this seed's own rows
-- (entered_by = 'claude-markets-2026-10-15') and never touches rows anyone else entered.
-- QA copy: infra/bigquery/qa/295_industry_benchmarks_seed_qa.sql writes the same rows
-- into mart_qa.ob1_industry_benchmarks. This file (prod) is NOT EXECUTED; needs owner OK.
-- =============================================================================

